WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.650
Instead of staring at your 
feet, look into my eyes

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.770
Please keep broadcasting.

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:11.490
Hey, everybody! Hands up!

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.490
Good job, Tamaki-kun.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:18.280
It's all you, So-chan.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.110
We're so small, and the clip's so short.

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.790
Why did you want to become an idol?

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.790
Why is Tamaki so obsessed with TV?

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:30.000
You're IDOLiSH7's Osaka Sogo 
and Yotsuba Tamaki, aren't you?

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:39.730
Sogo-kun and Tamaki-kun's 
popularity is on the rise.

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:42.020
60% of the fan mail we 
get is addressed to them.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:47.020
The two of them really stood out 
during the live concert broadcast.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:52.780
Fan Mail By Member

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:52.780
Osaka Sogo

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:52.780
Next popular after them is 
Riku-kun, then Iori-kun.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:58.580
The handsome Nagi-kun and leader Yamato-kun 
have a stable number of fans, too.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:03.040
That said, Mitsuki-kun's 
popularity is declining.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:06.090
A lot of people say he's 
their second favorite.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.290
I see.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.800
Differences in popularity within 
a group is a difficult problem.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:16.300
I wish we could promote them equally.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.970
LIVE X LIVE
 Broadcast

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:28.150
Gazing at the distant sky...

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:31.680
Someday we'll make it past there

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:37.310
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:44.120
We don't know what's right

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:47.330
So we Try and Jump!

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:50.500
Slamming face first into
challenges and laughing

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:54.130
For us It's Only Way!

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:57.320
Make it shake (For Your Sky)

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:00.820
Make it reach (For Your Heart)

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:03.310
We'll change any and all kinds of pain

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:04.470
Do Live! (Yeah!)

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:05.310
Live! (Yeah!)

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:08.730
In the light!

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.520
(One, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven Go!)

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:15.970
Yes Glory Days! Together 
we'll run through them

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:18.780
If your voice (Fuu!) reverberates (Dream!)

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.280
Then your wishes will become 
destiny (Singing New World!)

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:28.790
Give rise now to Age of Stage!

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:35.750
The future surely lies on the other side

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:38.670
Yes... It will keep on evolving

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:42.050
Our WiSH VOYAGE

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:48.310
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.030
Ray of Light

00:02:58.390 --> 00:02:59.030
What?

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.990
You want the two of us to debut together?

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:05.430
You both have everyone's
 attention right now.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:08.120
You'd become popular quickly 
if you were to debut.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.750
What do you think? It's a good deal.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:16.510
We appreciate the offer, but we're employed 
at our agency to debut with them.

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:17.170
So—

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.550
Does your debut have a date?

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.130
No, not yet.

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:23.650
I didn't think so.

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:25.380
It's a small agency.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:28.920
They don't have the money, connections, 
or knowledge to help you debut.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:34.520
We could introduce you to a good record 
company and give you a splendid debut.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.070
We're not doing it.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:40.840
Working with you means 
we can't work with them.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.410
We've worked with them until now.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.320
We won't work for you.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:47.370
Tamaki-kun.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.040
Are you sure?

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.910
You can't see your little sister while
 you're working for that agency.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:55.910
I believe her name was... Aya, correct?

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:58.270
How do you know that?

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.630
I did my research.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.520
What is he talking about?

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:08.130
My breath... Tricker!

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.230
Okay, good!

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:16.150
Good work!

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.630
Thank you.

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:23.450
Time flies.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.650
It always does at TV stations.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:29.290
Come in.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:32.660
Good work, boys.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:34.210
You were great today.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:37.050
We're counting on you at the Music Festa.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:39.750
Everyone's excited to see TRIGGER.

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:43.010
Sure. Thanks for having us again this year.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:48.010
Preparing for a ten hour broadcast
 every year must be difficult.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:51.180
Well, it is a monster program 
that features everything

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.060
from indie groups to major artists.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:56.390
Oh, right. Know any good performers?

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:58.610
We haven't decided which 
indie groups to feature yet.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.610
Huh?

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:03.290
Yotsuba Tamaki.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:05.970
You lost your mother to 
illness when you were young.

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:08.050
On top of that, your father is missing.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:10.610
You and your younger sister 
entered an orphanage.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:11.370
Huh?

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.240
Two years later,

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:17.140
only your sister was adopted by the 
president of a mid-sized company.

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:19.260
However, his company went bankrupt.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:23.510
His family disappeared overnight, 
and your sister disappeared with them.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:29.930
Aren't you trying to become an entertainer 
so you can be reunited with your sister?

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:32.250
Is that true, Tamaki-kun?

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.100
Is that why you're so desperate to be on TV?

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:38.820
I couldn't find her no 
matter how hard I tried.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:43.860
I thought she'd find me if 
my face showed up on TV.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:48.230
Your sister will be starting 
high school next year.

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:49.850
But they fled under the cover of night.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:52.530
Without any money, it'll be 
hard for her to go to school.

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:54.580
They'll probably put her to work.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.780
A 15-year-old girl unable 
to rely on her own family.

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:00.710
Poor girl.

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:04.590
I'll find her. We'll live together.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:09.050
But isn't your current agency more 
important to you than your sister?

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:10.510
I—

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:13.280
Tamaki-kun, you don't have 
to listen to him anymore.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:14.010
Let's go.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.560
Excuse us, Yaotome-san.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:22.610
Tamaki-kun?

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:26.610
If I debut with you, will you put me on TV?

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:27.530
Huh?!

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:29.140
Of course.

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:32.650
Once you're in a commercial, your 
face will be on TV every day.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:35.910
I promise I'll pay you however much 
you need to live with your sister.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:39.190
Don't, Tamaki-kun!

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:40.080
Don't listen to him!

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.050
Tamaki-kun!

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:50.090
But debuting with Osaka 
Sogo-kun is our condition.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:51.640
No, thank you.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.140
Tamaki-kun, let's go.

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:56.010
You can give me your answer another time.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.580
But you should hurry.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:01.770
My mind has a tendency to change easily.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:10.030
So-chan...

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:18.530
Sogo-san.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:20.500
No.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.350
Please!

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:26.210
Transfer to their agency with me!

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:28.210
I can't.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:29.470
Please!

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:30.850
Stop this!

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:32.680
No point in being polite now.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:35.870
She's the only sister I have!

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:39.010
I feel sorry for the others, 
but I have to help her!

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:42.100
Come on, please! Debut with me!

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:49.970
I see. So that's what happened...

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:54.330
I don't think Tamaki-kun 
actually wants to transfer,

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:58.620
but their president said 
things to agitate him.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:03.610
Manager, are we still not ready to debut?

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:08.500
Debuting would assuage
 Tamaki-kun's concerns.

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:11.670
You're right...

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:15.160
What?! What the hell are you talking about?!

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:16.650
What does that mean?!

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:18.350
What do you mean, you're quitting?!

00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:21.520
No! Don't fight.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.680
Oh...

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:27.020
Sorry, guys.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:28.920
I don't want an apology!

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:32.580
Did Sogo say he's going to debut
 with another agency, too?!

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.030
Sorry.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.350
What's going on?

00:08:35.350 --> 00:08:37.570
Wait a second, did you tell the others?!

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:44.000
I thought I should apologize...

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.000
Y-You idiot! Why'd you have to jump the gun?!

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.890
There's a proper order to these things!

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:52.340
I thought I should apologize for you, too!

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.420
Don't apologize for me!

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:58.990
Hey, So, Tama. Are you guys 
serious about quitting?

00:08:58.990 --> 00:08:59.680
Sorry.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:00.280
No!

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:01.180
Which is it?!

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:04.730
Why don't you quit, then?

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:05.060
Huh?

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:06.610
Iori!

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:11.820
Osaka-san hasn't, but this means Yotsuba-san 
has already forsaken IDOLiSH7.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.080
Then we should forsake him.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:17.160
We don't need you, either.

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:21.450
Go ahead. Leave.

00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:25.510
That's going too far, Iori!

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:30.360
Tamaki, there must be some 
reason for this. Right?

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:36.130
Please, Tamaki. Tell us why.

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:40.510
Tamaki-kun, they should know the truth.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:43.430
If you can't tell them, I can do it for you.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:48.120
What the hell's going on?! Tell us!

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:53.830
I have a younger sister.

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:56.280
We grew up in an orphanage together.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.870
But we haven't seen each 
other for a long time.

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:01.990
I'm still looking for her, 
but I can't find her.

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:03.050
Huh?

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:04.660
A young girl is missing?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:08.670
If I don't find her soon, she 
won't be able to go to school.

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:15.140
They might put her to work, 
so I wanted her to find me.

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:16.670
I wanted to be on TV.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:21.600
So I thought I'd transfer to an agency 
that would let me debut sooner.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:24.260
What kind of reason is that?

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:26.470
You should've started with that!

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:27.500
S-Sorry!

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:29.650
You're terrible at explanations!

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:32.400
Of course we'd be surprised 
at your sudden announcement!

00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:34.400
Unbelievable.

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:36.630
That's enough.

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:41.010
It's all right, Tamaki.

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:44.120
In other words, it's okay as 
long as you can appear on TV?

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:45.790
Yes.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:47.330
Good!

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:51.210
In that case, the seven of 
us should debut together!

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:52.460
What?

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:56.320
Our songs, our fans.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:58.770
We have so much more now.

00:10:58.770 --> 00:11:00.720
We can debut!

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:04.350
Should you be making that decision, Nagi?

00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:07.320
Negotiating with the president, huh?

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:08.930
Let's give it a shot, Manager.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:12.850
Yeah. I'll make an appointment immediately.

00:11:14.550 --> 00:11:16.670
Our debut, huh?

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:19.070
I wonder what the president will say.

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:20.030
Sure.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:21.280
What?

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:23.450
I was thinking about suggesting it.

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:24.990
Really?

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:28.070
Yeah. I think now's the right time.

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:31.870
And if Yaotome's making a move, 
then we can't afford to take our time.

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:35.880
Osaka Sogo-kun.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:37.090
Yes!

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:38.630
Yotsuba Tamaki-kun.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:39.760
Yeah.

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:44.390
The two of you will debut.

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:47.930
What?

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:49.430
Just the two of them?

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:51.480
What about us?

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.080
What are you talking about, Dad?

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:55.360
Have you given up on 
promoting all seven of us?

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:59.320
I'm sorry. The president likes 
to test people sometimes.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:04.950
Right? You don't actually intend to 
debut just the two of them, right?

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:11.080
I wish I could have taken my time 
to debut all seven of you together.

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:14.850
However, Yaotome has set his sights on you.

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:16.710
He's merciless.

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:18.610
If he can't have you,

00:12:18.610 --> 00:12:22.060
he'll do something to destroy you so 
completely you'll never work again.

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:27.090
In order to protect you and IDOLiSH7,

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:29.470
I'm sorry, but I have to separate you.

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:36.740
So you'll debut them to keep us safe.

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:41.320
We'll continue developing the rest of you 
until you're ready as originally planned.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:42.740
When we're ready?

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:46.700
Once everyone knows you as well as them.

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:51.400
Is there any other way?

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:52.910
I don't want this.

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:54.870
I don't want to leave my friends.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:56.370
Sogo-san.

00:12:57.140 --> 00:12:59.100
I know it's hard, but you'll 
have to get over it.

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:02.470
In a few years, you may be 
able to work together again.

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:04.130
A few years?

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:05.540
That long?

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:06.990
Fine.

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:07.760
Huh?

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:11.480
But first, give us a chance.

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:16.770
If we can reach the level of recognition 
you're looking for, let us debut as seven.

00:13:17.140 --> 00:13:18.560
Yamato-san.

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:23.010
In other words,

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:26.480
the five of us will have to raise our own 
recognition in a short amount of time.

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:28.950
Can we really do that?

00:13:33.130 --> 00:13:34.730
Sir, it's an emergency!

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:36.330
Huh? You're all here.

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:38.170
What is it, Banri-kun?

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:43.960
IDOLiSH7 has been asked to 
appear at the Music Festa.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:45.880
Huh?

00:13:48.230 --> 00:13:50.430
The Music Festa?

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:53.050
They hold it every year.

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:58.350
They get a bunch of indie and major artists 
together for a ten hour live show!

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:01.280
It's not a local station or
 late night show, either.

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:03.990
It's a highly rated program 
on a national network!

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:06.740
I have no complaints about this big chance!

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:07.460
Yeah.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:11.200
When one door shuts, another one opens.

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:15.330
If the Music Festa goes well, 
can the seven of us debut?

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:17.730
We have a plan.

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:19.500
Sir, please.

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:22.040
Please.

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:31.550
<i>That night is coming back!</i>

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:35.560
<i>The annual music festival...</i>

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:35.560
Strawberries

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.560
<i>Music Festa!</i>

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:41.930
<i>The performance of your dreams
 from a splendid series of artists!</i>

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:45.640
<i>Don't miss the ten hour live broadcast!</i>

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:49.740
Huh? Really?!

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:52.090
What? Did something happen?

00:14:52.090 --> 00:14:55.070
I7 is going to be on Music Festa!

00:14:55.070 --> 00:14:56.400
I7?

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:58.160
IDOLiSH7!

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:01.610
Oh, those unpopular idols you like.

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:03.030
They're plenty popular!

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:04.690
They're good at singing and handsome!

00:15:04.690 --> 00:15:07.220
They even sold out their outdoor show!

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:09.190
I'm so happy!

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:11.640
I need to tell everyone.

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:14.970
Really? If they're going to be
 on TV, maybe I'll watch.

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:17.670
Yeah, you should!

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:21.060
You'll definitely become their fans!

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:28.610
What's the meaning of this, Takanashi?

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:30.570
What kind of connections did he use?!

00:15:30.980 --> 00:15:34.570
How unusual for you to raise your voice.

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:36.990
Do you have some kind of 
grudge against that agency?

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:38.200
It's none of your business!

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:41.370
Going somewhere?

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:43.260
I have the afternoon off.

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:45.130
I can go wherever I want.

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:47.960
You're going back to her store?

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:49.300
Stop acting so disgraceful!

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:52.040
It's none of your business.

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:55.010
Excuse me.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:03.060
Um, did you listen to the song 
sample I sent you the other day?

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:04.890
I certainly did.

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:07.070
How dare you send me this garbage.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:09.030
Garbage?

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:11.090
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:16:11.090 --> 00:16:13.570
Bring me a song worthy of TRIGGER!

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:15.570
If you can't, you're fired!

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:16.990
I'm sorry!

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:21.510
If you don't want to lose your job, 
bring me a song better than IDOLiSH7's.

00:16:21.510 --> 00:16:23.690
Huh? IDOLiSH7?

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:25.850
I could replace you in a heartbeat!

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:27.670
Remember that!

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.300
I'll rewrite it immediately!

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:30.760
Excuse me!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.600
Their intensity is in their music, too.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:38.920
Who the hell is writing them?

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:40.710
Damn you, IDOLiSH7.

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:48.580
IDOLiSH7...

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:55.910
I'm giving you a new song.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:56.700
Huh?

00:16:56.700 --> 00:17:02.450
Untitled

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:59.440
It's different from the others.

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:03.670
It's a slower song that speaks 
to the hearts of its listeners.

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:09.380
Your harmony, and bringing your 
feelings together will be important.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:13.300
Make your hearts one, and 
take hold of your future.

00:17:13.610 --> 00:17:14.880
Yes, sir!

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:27.540
It's a nice song.

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:30.150
Untitled

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:33.150
We still don't know who's writing these.

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:36.570
Something wrong?

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:37.860
Ah, nothing.

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:43.210
This will make the dancing slow, too.

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:44.620
Sounds difficult.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:48.020
We can't hide behind intensity.

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:50.630
We'll have to execute each move perfectly.

00:17:50.990 --> 00:17:52.740
The same goes for the music.

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:57.300
Given the softness of the melody, it'll 
be unconvincing unless it's sung well.

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:00.090
You have to sing this right.

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:02.720
Don't mess this up, Nanase-san.

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:04.750
Don't pressure me like that!

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:06.640
Don't blame me if I have an asthma attack!

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:09.440
You've gotten defiant.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:10.980
I guess.

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:14.370
Overlapping the melodies 
correctly will be hard.

00:18:14.370 --> 00:18:17.070
Even if I'm distracted, 
I can't cover my ears.

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:18.150
Yeah.

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:21.890
So and Tama, your voices are 
nice when you're harmonizing.

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:25.680
Yeah. You finally found a way we get along.

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:27.190
You're finally being honest.

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:29.870
I'm surprised you wanted to debut with me.

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:32.790
You gotta do what you gotta do.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:34.380
Do you have to phrase it like that?

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:37.840
I'll have to practice even harder.

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:40.340
I don't want to get left behind by you guys.

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:41.300
Mitsuki-san.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:45.480
Becoming an idol has been 
my dream since I was a kid,

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:47.640
but it's more than that now.

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:50.220
I want the seven of us to work together.

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:52.920
I don't want to be left behind 
or leave anyone else behind.

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:54.610
Don't you guys agree?

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:55.650
Yes!

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:56.990
Of course.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:57.940
Yeah.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:02.660
I know the conditions are tough, 
but this is our national debut.

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:05.730
Let's pull ourselves together 
and really pump things up!

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:06.700
I agree.

00:19:07.130 --> 00:19:09.940
I should practice looking into the camera.

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:11.790
You do that.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:18.260
As long as we're having fun, I'm sure 
the gods will tell us to stay together.

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:19.590
Yeah!

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:40.850
Hey.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:47.400
I feel like I've gotten pretty 
good, but it's still not 100%.

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:49.110
Damn it!

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:53.420
Things feel different when you have energy.

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:55.970
Wh-Where did that come from?

00:19:55.970 --> 00:19:59.760
I'm always overflowing with energy 
no matter when or where I am.

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:02.120
You were worried, weren't you?

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:05.570
What's wrong with that?

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:08.030
I don't want to get left behind.

00:20:08.030 --> 00:20:13.320
I know I don't have any exceptional 
talent like everyone else does.

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:16.360
Everyone's glad to have you around, Mitsu.

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:19.850
Uh, oh man.

00:20:19.850 --> 00:20:21.740
Some kinda liquid's coming out of my eyes!

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:24.610
You idiot.

00:20:26.710 --> 00:20:28.340
That's me!

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:33.890
I want to make my dream come true.

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:35.810
I really do.

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:37.590
Please, God.

00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:43.200
<i>Let's go Wake me up! <Can't wake up></i>

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:46.910
<i>Let's dream together <Anywhere></i>

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:50.700
<i>Twilight for the two of us <Swaying></i>

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:50.700
Tenn-nii...

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:52.600
<i>I just fall in you</i>

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:52.600
You're watching it again?

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:54.370
<i>I just fall in you</i>

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:54.890
Iori.

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:58.190
<i>Swirling red Lightning</i>

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:58.190
What's with you?

00:20:58.190 --> 00:20:59.830
At least knock—

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:01.570
<i>I'll give you sweet memories</i>

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:01.070
You don't need to watch this anymore.

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:04.230
Hey! What do you think you're doing?

00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:06.680
Stop chasing Kujo Tenn's shadow.

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:07.600
Huh?

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:10.330
Nanase-san, you should sing your own songs.

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:12.750
I promise I'll make you a superstar.

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:13.560
Huh?

00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:15.410
You will?

00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:18.740
With the manager.

00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:21.090
Rather, mostly the manager.

00:21:22.580 --> 00:21:23.340
Okay...

00:21:24.210 --> 00:21:28.300
With your singing ability, I know we 
can satisfy the president's condition.

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:31.770
Even if you don't believe in me, 
believe in my management skills—

00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:35.020
no, my analytical abilities.

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:43.810
So, this is where legends are born.

00:21:49.030 --> 00:22:00.540
If even a small beat of my wings 
can raise me up from nothing...

00:22:04.650 --> 00:22:10.050
Haruki, I didn't think I'd become 
so emotionally invested in them.

00:22:10.790 --> 00:22:14.560
Please cast a spell on us again.

00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:19.210
Give us the power to cause a miracle.

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:37.950
Start running (beyond)

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:44.960
Your imagination... Alive

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:58.610
If you desire something from 
the bottom of your heart

00:22:58.610 --> 00:23:03.360
Risk your life and dive in

00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:08.440
The resolve to discard what's truly important

00:23:08.440 --> 00:23:13.570
Is the boat that will take you to new sights

00:23:13.570 --> 00:23:16.120
(Hey man!) Take the strings of your heart

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:18.660
(Hey man!) And stretch them

00:23:18.660 --> 00:23:21.540
(Say dream!) To the limit

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:26.460
At the other end you're sure 
to find the Gate to paradise

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:32.450
You'll be the first witness

00:23:32.450 --> 00:23:37.240
Our pounding pulses are Heavenly

00:23:37.240 --> 00:23:42.270
Admit that you can't deny it

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:46.730
We start... What do your fingertips

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:51.260
Seek now?
